From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: built-in Texture Pool x2 game patch for the later-area freeze with Max Resolution on (Lichii #1313, RsMan-Dev's patch), EDEN_UP_OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_X2=1, off by default

What: with Max Resolution (EDEN_NX2_OOT_MAX_RESOLUTION=1, on in our play settings) the
render targets outgrow the first pool of the game's own graphics allocator. In one building of a
later area the game then reads through a null allocation and freezes (endless unmapped reads).
Upstream: 3 of 3 freezes before, none in 2 runs after (Linux PC, 2x, Max Resolution on).

The game patch: main+0xC2A36C (stp x8, x9, [sp, #0x10]) stores the first pool size (x8) and the
growth block size (x9) into the allocator's init descriptor. It becomes `bl` to a cave at
main+0x3C462C0 (zero padding after .text) that runs `lsl x8, x8, #1; stp x8, x9, [sp, #0x10];
ret`. So the first pool is twice as big. Same bytes as upstream, added to our group-patch table
(applied all or none: the original word and an all-zero cave are checked, and a user mod at either
place wins). Our table gets upstream's test that a cave lies in the padding after .text, inside
.text's last page and before .rodata (a new field, false for the existing records).

Price: the game's first graphics pool is twice as big. How many MiB is not in the code (it is the
game's own number in x8; not checked). On a base PS5 that is guest memory taken at start, in a
memory that already runs out at area loads. So off by default; only worth it with Max Resolution on
and only for that later area, or to test whether a pool that is too small plays a part in our
area-load crashes.

Switch: EDEN_UP_OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_X2=1 (exact "1"), read once at game load. Off: nothing changes.
Only for the Ocarina build id E0F3CCFAF50065AE4EA01EB5AEB13B1A45DA3348.

Test: the boot log says `Applying built-in patch "Texture Pool x2 (built-in)" (2 sites in main)`.
Compare the memory lines at start and at the first area load with and without it. Not checked:
compile and run; whether the game saves x30 before main+0xC2A36C (the `bl` overwrites x30;
upstream ran it without trouble, so most likely yes).

Origin and credit: RsMan-Dev's Texture Pool x2 patch (described in zortos293/Lichii #247), built in
by William RICHER (RsMan-Dev) in zortos293/Lichii 12062785e3 (#1313, co-author Devin Alsup).
---
diff --git a/src/core/file_sys/patch_manager.cpp b/src/core/file_sys/patch_manager.cpp
index 18b6498..86bddfb 100644
--- a/src/core/file_sys/patch_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/core/file_sys/patch_manager.cpp
@@ -128,6 +128,9 @@ struct BuiltinPatchRecord {
     size_t module_offset;
     std::span<const u8> bytes;
     std::span<const u8> original;
+    /// 0748: a code cave that must lie in the zero padding after .text, inside its last page
+    /// and before .rodata (upstream's test, zortos293/Lichii 12062785e3).
+    bool executable_padding = false;
 };
 
 struct BuiltinGroupPatch {
@@ -291,6 +294,29 @@ constexpr std::array OOT_POLL_BACKOFF_RECORDS{
     BuiltinPatchRecord{0x17088, OOT_POLL_BACKOFF_CAVE, OOT_POLL_PADDING_ORIGINAL},
 };
 
+// EDEN_UP_OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_X2=1 (exact "1"; 0748): RsMan-Dev's Texture Pool x2 patch as built in
+// by Lichii #1313 (William RICHER, 12062785e3). With Max Resolution the render targets outgrow the
+// game's graphics allocator's first pool, and one later-area building then reads through a null
+// allocation and the game freezes. main+0xC2A36C (stp x8, x9, [sp, #0x10]) stores the first pool
+// size (x8) and the growth block size (x9) into the allocator's init descriptor; it becomes a call
+// of a cave at main+0x3C462C0 that doubles x8 first (lsl x8, x8, #1; stp; ret).
+[[nodiscard]] bool TexturePoolX2Enabled() {
+    static const bool enabled = UpSwitch("EDEN_UP_OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_X2");
+    return enabled;
+}
+constexpr std::array<u8, 4> OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_ORIGINAL{0xE8, 0x27, 0x01, 0xA9}; // stp x8, x9, [sp, #0x10]
+constexpr std::array<u8, 4> OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_CALL{0xD5, 0x6F, 0xC0, 0x94};     // bl 0x3c462c0
+constexpr std::array<u8, 12> OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_CAVE_ORIGINAL{};
+constexpr std::array<u8, 12> OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_CAVE{
+    0x08, 0xF9, 0x7F, 0xD3, // lsl x8, x8, #1
+    0xE8, 0x27, 0x01, 0xA9, // stp x8, x9, [sp, #0x10]
+    0xC0, 0x03, 0x5F, 0xD6, // ret
+};
+constexpr std::array OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_RECORDS{
+    BuiltinPatchRecord{0xC2A36C, OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_CALL, OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_ORIGINAL},
+    BuiltinPatchRecord{0x3C462C0, OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_CAVE, OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_CAVE_ORIGINAL, true},
+};
+
 constexpr std::array BUILTIN_GROUP_PATCHES{
     BuiltinGroupPatch{"Native zstd (built-in)", 0x0400486024DEC000, "main",
                       "E0F3CCFAF50065AE4EA01EB5AEB13B1A45DA3348", OOT_NATIVE_ZSTD_RECORDS,
@@ -304,6 +330,9 @@ constexpr std::array BUILTIN_GROUP_PATCHES{
     BuiltinGroupPatch{"Resource poll backoff (built-in)", 0x0400486024DEC000, "main",
                       "E0F3CCFAF50065AE4EA01EB5AEB13B1A45DA3348", OOT_POLL_BACKOFF_RECORDS,
                       PollBackoffEnabled},
+    BuiltinGroupPatch{"Texture Pool x2 (built-in)", 0x0400486024DEC000, "main",
+                      "E0F3CCFAF50065AE4EA01EB5AEB13B1A45DA3348", OOT_TEXTURE_POOL_RECORDS,
+                      TexturePoolX2Enabled},
 };
 
 // `nso` is the module as loaded, `out` the same with the user's mods applied. A patch is applied
@@ -336,6 +365,24 @@ void ApplyBuiltinGroupPatches(std::vector<u8>& out, const std::vector<u8>& nso,
                 break;
             }
             const size_t offset = sizeof(Loader::NSOHeader) + record.module_offset;
+            if (record.executable_padding) {
+                // 0748: the cave must be executable and unused: zero bytes after .text, before
+                // the end of .text's last page and before .rodata.
+                Loader::NSOHeader header{};
+                std::memcpy(&header, nso.data(), sizeof(header));
+                const auto& text = header.segments[0];
+                const u64 text_end = u64{text.location} + text.size;
+                const u64 executable_end = (text_end + 0xFFF) & ~u64{0xFFF};
+                const u64 cave_end = u64{record.module_offset} + record.bytes.size();
+                if (record.module_offset < text_end || cave_end > executable_end ||
+                    cave_end > header.segments[1].location) {
+                    LOG_WARNING(Loader,
+                                "    - Skipping \"{}\": code cave {}+{:#x} is not executable padding",
+                                patch.name, name, record.module_offset);
+                    apply = false;
+                    break;
+                }
+            }
             if (!std::equal(record.original.begin(), record.original.end(), nso.begin() + offset)) {
                 LOG_WARNING(Loader, "    - Skipping \"{}\": unexpected original bytes at {}+{:#x}",
                             patch.name, name, record.module_offset);
